CAT = "aesiraRole"; SEG = "ROL"
Q = [
("A Dubai shopping mall hires licensed guards. What is their main purpose on site?",
 "Protect people and property", ["Enforce traffic fines on roads", "Fully investigate crimes", "Replace Dubai Police patrols"],
 "A security guard protects lives and property by deterring, detecting and reporting. Investigating crimes and enforcing the law belong to Dubai Police."),
("Site instructions written for one particular post, telling the guard what to do there, are called:",
 "Assignment instructions", ["A job advertisement form", "A visitor sign-in log", "A licence condition"],
 "Assignment instructions (also called post orders) set out the duties, patrol times, contacts and procedures for a specific site."),
("A guard starting the night shift should first:",
 "Get a handover from the last guard", ["Begin a patrol without any briefing", "Check social media for news", "Sign the log for both guards"],
 "A handover passes on open incidents, faults, keys and expected visitors, so nothing is lost between shifts. Signing for another guard falsifies the record."),
("A guard is due to be relieved at 7 a.m. but the relief guard has not arrived. What should the guard do?",
 "Stay and call the supervisor", ["Lock the site and go home", "Leave the keys at reception", "Ask a cleaner to cover the post"],
 "A post must not be left unguarded. The guard stays and tells the supervisor, who arranges cover. An unlicensed person cannot stand in."),
("A resident offers a guard an expensive watch for 'looking after' their car park space. The guard should:",
 "Decline it and tell the supervisor", ["Accept it if under a set value", "Accept and share with colleagues", "Accept but log it as lost property"],
 "Gifts given for special treatment create a conflict of interest and breach integrity rules. The guard declines and reports it so it is on record."),
("Why does a professional appearance in the full uniform matter on a Dubai post?",
 "It deters crime and reassures", ["It makes patrols much faster", "It allows entry to any building", "It replaces the SIRA card"],
 "A smart, visible guard deters offenders and reassures the public. The uniform never replaces the SIRA card, which must also be displayed."),
("A tourist asks a mall guard for directions while the guard is watching an exit. The best response is to:",
 "Help briefly while staying alert", ["Ignore the tourist, but politely", "Leave the post to walk them there", "Ask them to call the police"],
 "Good customer service is part of the role, but the guard keeps watching the post. Leaving it uncovered defeats the reason the guard is there."),
("A guard finds a colleague asleep in the control room. What is the right action?",
 "Wake them and report it", ["Take a photo and post it", "Let them sleep until dawn", "Cover for them in the log"],
 "Sleeping on duty leaves the site unprotected. The guard wakes the colleague and reports to the supervisor; covering it up makes the guard part of the breach."),
("Which of these is part of a guard's duty of care toward the public?",
 "Warning people of a known hazard", ["Arresting anyone who is rude", "Searching everyone on entry", "Keeping lost children at the post"],
 "A guard who spots a wet floor or a broken step must warn people and report it. Search and detention powers are limited and never apply to rudeness."),
("Dubai has residents of many nationalities. How should a guard deal with every visitor?",
 "With equal respect and courtesy", ["By nationality, as a priority", "By how smartly they are dressed", "By the language they speak"],
 "Treating people differently because of nationality, religion or appearance is discrimination. Professional conduct means the same standard for everyone."),
("A guard must report to a supervisor through the chain of command. This means the guard should:",
 "Report to the supervisor first", ["Contact the company owner first", "Email SIRA about every task", "Ask the client for orders"],
 "Normally the guard reports to the immediate supervisor, who escalates. Emergencies still go straight to 999, 998 or 997."),
("Which item should a guard check is working at the start of every shift?",
 "The radio or phone", ["The vending machine", "The client's computer", "The lift music system"],
 "A guard who cannot call for help is a hazard. Radios are tested and batteries checked at handover, and faults are logged."),
("Under SIRA rules a security company must keep a duty officer available around the clock for which activity?",
 "General guarding", ["Office cleaning teams", "Car rental", "Valet parking"],
 "Art. 16(19) of the 2026 bylaw requires a duty officer available 24 hours a day, every day, for general guarding, cash transport, control rooms, vehicle tracking, tourist sites, events and bodyguards."),
("A guard uses the site's master key card to enter an office out of curiosity. This is:",
 "Misuse of trust and access", ["Acceptable during a patrol", "Allowed if nothing is taken", "A normal security check"],
 "Keys and cards are given for duty purposes only. Entering areas without a duty reason breaches integrity and the site's trust."),
("A guard is asked by a friend to let them use the residents' gym without a pass. The guard should:",
 "Refuse and apply the access rule", ["Allow it outside busy hours", "Allow it once as a favour", "Ask any resident to sign them in"],
 "Rules apply to everyone, friends included. Bending access control for favours is a conflict of interest and weakens the site's security."),
("A guard is on a 12-hour shift and feels very tired. What is the safest action?",
 "Tell the supervisor straight away", ["Sleep briefly in the car park", "Drink energy drinks all night", "Leave the post for a walk to wake up"],
 "Fatigue reduces alertness. The supervisor can arrange a break or relief; sleeping or leaving the post on one's own decision leaves the site unguarded."),
("A guard notices a recurring fault: a fire exit door at a labour accommodation no longer latches. The guard should:",
 "Log it and report it", ["Tie it shut with rope", "Ignore it as a maintenance job", "Wedge it open for airflow"],
 "Faults found on patrol are logged and reported until fixed. Tying or wedging a fire door creates a danger in a fire."),
("Which statement about private security and Dubai Police is correct?",
 "Guards support the police", ["Guards outrank police on site", "Guards can issue police fines", "Police need guard permission"],
 "Private guards prevent and report and then cooperate with the police, who have the legal authority to investigate and enforce."),
("Which behaviour by a guard may lead people to think the guard is a police officer?",
 "Calling themselves 'police'", ["Wearing the SIRA-approved uniform", "Showing the SIRA card", "Giving clear directions"],
 "Guards must never present themselves as police or an official security authority. The approved uniform and card show they are licensed private security."),
("A guard on a hotel lobby post is offered a seat in a quiet back office. Why should the guard refuse?",
 "The post must stay visible", ["Seats are not allowed by law", "The office has no air conditioning", "Hotels charge for the seat"],
 "A guard's value comes from visible presence and observation of the area. A hidden guard neither deters nor sees what happens."),
("A visitor shouts at a guard over a parking rule. What is the guard's best first response?",
 "Stay calm and listen", ["Shout back to show control", "Walk away without a word", "Threaten to call SIRA"],
 "Listening calmly lowers tension and often ends the dispute. Raising the voice escalates it. If threats begin, the guard asks for help."),
("A security company is short of staff and asks a guard's unlicensed friend to cover one night shift. Under the 2026 bylaw this is:",
 "Not allowed without a licence", ["Allowed for a single shift", "Allowed if a guard supervises", "Allowed if the client agrees"],
 "Art. 16 forbids a provider from appointing anyone to provide security who does not hold a valid SIRA licence, or who is not its contracted employee registered in SIRA's systems."),
("A guard notices a manager's assistant regularly removing boxes at midnight. The guard should:",
 "Record it and report it", ["Ignore it as staff business", "Confront and search them", "Post about it on social media"],
 "Unusual patterns are reported with facts (time, what was seen) to the supervisor. Searching without consent or policy is not the guard's right."),
("Professional radio use means a guard should:",
 "Keep messages short and clear", ["Chat freely to stay alert", "Use their own made-up slang codes", "Share guest names openly"],
 "Radio channels are for operations. Short, clear messages keep the channel free for emergencies, and private details are not broadcast."),
]
